message: "If you use ReflectoGen, please cite the archived software release and the associated SoftwareX article when available."
title: "ReflectoGen: Physics-Inspired and Calibration-Enabled Reflectogram Synthesis for Pile Integrity Testing"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/canbula/ReflectoGen"
url: "https://github.com/canbula/ReflectoGen"
authors:
  - family-names: Canbula
    given-names: Bora
    email: bora.canbula@cbu.edu.tr
  - family-names: Öztürk
    given-names: Övünç
  - family-names: Özacar
    given-names: Vehbi
  - family-names: Özacar
    given-names: Tuğba
abstract: >-
  ReflectoGen is a calibration-enabled, physics-inspired Python software package
  for generating synthetic reflectograms for low-strain pile integrity testing.
  It supports single-case generation, batch dataset construction, optional
  waveform/profile CSV export, and archive-based calibration of global generator
  parameters.
keywords:
  - low-strain pile integrity testing
  - reflectogram synthesis
  - synthetic data
  - calibration-enabled software
  - Python
